{{also|wörden}}
==Dutch==

===Etymology===
{{root|nl|ine-pro|*wert-}}
From {{inh|nl|dum|werden}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|werthan}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*werþan}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*werþaną}}, from {{inh|nl|ine-pro|*wértti}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈʋɔrdə(n)/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-worden.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|wor|den}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɔrdən|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{nl-verb}}

# {{lb|nl|copulative}} to [[become]], to [[get]], to [[grow]], to [[turn]]
#: {{syn|nl|komen|q=Belgium}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Zij wilde altijd al lerares '''worden'''.|She always wanted to become a teacher.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Mijn broer '''wordt''' vandaag twintig.|My brother is turning twenty today.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Het '''wordt''' hier erg benauwd. Open de ramen alsjeblieft!|It's getting very stuffy in here. Please open the windows!}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Morgen '''wordt''' het twintig graden.|It '''will be''' twenty degrees tomorrow.}}
# {{lb|nl|transitive|auxiliary}} {{n-g|Used to form the [[imperfect tense]] of the [[passive voice]], together with a [[past participle]].}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Ze '''worden''' gered.|They are being saved.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|De muur '''werd''' geschilderd.|The wall was being painted.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|De muur zal '''worden''' geschilderd.|The wall will be painted. / The wall is going to be painted.}}

====Usage notes====
* The [[perfect tense]] passive is formed using {{m|nl|zijn}}, while ''worden'' matches English [[continuous]] constructions in meaning. Therefore, as in usage 2 above,
*# ''Ze '''worden''' gered.'' translates to “They '''are being''' saved.”
*# ''Ze '''werden''' gered''. translates to “They '''were being''' saved.”
*# Consequently, ''Ze '''''zijn''''' gered.'' and ''Ze '''''waren''''' gered.'' would be translated as “They '''have been''' saved.” and “They '''had been''' saved.” respectively.

